  "sourceHeading": "MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS – AIR AMBULANCE SERVICE (CHECKLIST)",
  "sourcePages": [70, 71, 72, 73],
  "notes": "This section is the manual's own explicit checklist, organised into five numbered inspection areas: 1 Management and Administration, 2 Aviation Regulations Compliance, 3 Patient Handling Equipment, 4 Flight Crew Qualifications and Fitness, 5 Facilities. Each area is a table with the item number, the checklist question/requirement, a 'REQUIRES ACTION' column with YES/NO tick boxes, and a 'COMMENT/FINDING' free-text column — note the distinct response semantics: the YES/NO records whether the item REQUIRES ACTION (i.e. YES = deficiency found), not whether the requirement is met; the COMMENT/FINDING column captures the inspector's finding. This is mapped to responseType STATUS for every item. Each area's preamble states: 'The following checklist items are provided for guidance and should be used during the Inspection.' Area 3 (Patient Handling Equipment) additionally states: 'This is a minimum requirement list.' The manual's own item numbers are preserved in sourceItemNumber; AAM-### codes are additional stable codes, not replacements. Page 70 numbers two consecutive items '1-04' (quality assurance program, and AHPCZ registered practitioner in-charge) before continuing at 1-05 — this duplicate numbering is preserved as printed and flagged reviewRequired on the second occurrence. Item 1-09 cross-references Inspection Area 5 and item 2-02 cross-references item 1-07; both cross-references are kept verbatim inside the requirement text.",
